  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two points <math><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi></math> are lying on the curve&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> <em>in</em> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math> plane such that <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>⋅</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>⋅</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, then the value of&nbsp;<math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is</p>\r\r<p>(where,&nbsp;<math><mi>O</mi></math> is the origin)</p>\r",
